Subject: [PATCH] subsystem_restart: restart the modem on its own when it crashes

Every Qualcomm subsystem (modem, audio DSP, WiFi core, video core) started with the
restart level SYSTEM: if one crashed, the kernel restarted the whole tablet. Stock set
the modem's to RELATED from user space (ssr_setup, persist.sys.ssr.restart_level=modem),
so a modem crash cost only the mobile connection for a few seconds.

A property in the device tree does the same here, read when the subsystem registers:
the modem's node carries it, the others keep SYSTEM as on stock. Doing it from init
would mean writing to /sys/bus/msm_subsys/devices/subsysN, whose number only reflects
the order in which the drivers happened to start.
---
--- arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/msm8956.dtsi
+++ arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/msm8956.dtsi
@@ -2150,6 +2150,7 @@
 
 	qcom,mss@4080000 {
 		compatible = "qcom,pil-q6v55-mss";
+		qcom,restart-level-related;
 		reg = <0x04080000 0x100>,
 		      <0x0194f000 0x010>,
 		      <0x01950000 0x008>,
--- drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c
+++ drivers/soc/qcom/subsystem_restart.c
@@ -1597,6 +1597,13 @@ struct subsys_device *subsys_register(struct subsys_desc *desc)
 	}
 	dev_set_name(&subsys->dev, "subsys%d", subsys->id);
 
+	/*
+	 * A subsystem marked so in the device tree restarts on its own when it
+	 * crashes, instead of taking the whole system down with it.
+	 */
+	if (ofnode && of_property_read_bool(ofnode, "qcom,restart-level-related"))
+		subsys->restart_level = RESET_SUBSYS_COUPLED;
+
 	mutex_init(&subsys->track.lock);
 
 	ret = subsys_debugfs_add(subsys);
